1. COMPACTNESS: Differentiates between compact and elongated shapes. Its range [73, 119], with distinct quartiles, may separate vehicle types with sharper or more rounded silhouettes.
2. CIRCULARITY: Highlights shapes closer to circles or irregularly shaped silhouettes. Its range [33, 59] suggests variability suited to detecting differences in broadness.
3. DISTANCE_CIRCULARITY: Indicates uniformity in edge distance, useful for classifying vehicles with smoother versus jagged outlines (range [40, 110]).
